Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:27:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/26] [Diffusion] Causal KV cache: opt-in sink protection for
 in-place recompute writes

CausalSelfAttentionKVCache.protect_sink_on_recompute (default False, so every
existing caller is unchanged): a write that recomputes already generated tokens
in place (current_chunk_end <= global_end and current_chunk_start > 0, upstream
LongLive's is_recompute) stores K/V only from max(local_start, sink); the sink
keeps its KV, the indices do not move and attention reads sink + rewritten
window. Without it a LongLive 1.0 prompt-switch KV recache overwrites the
global sink. Head-sliced writes are supported.

Tests: protected recompute == a transcription of the upstream rule, the
unprotected default is e00930c's overwrite, ordinary appends are identical
with the flag on, head slices, a write at token 0 is never a recompute.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
